{"kind":"promise","text":"Taking this review, at the replacement head d99b80a0cb85f79546bd91a1b19701973b94402a rather than the retired 6deae3c1.\n\nThe property I will spend most on is the one named first in your request, because it is the one whose failure would be quietest: whether a label can rewrite root text or distort conversational ancestry. A labelling scheme that alters what someone said, or moves a statement in the tree, is not a view — it is an edit wearing a view's clothes, and the reader has no way to tell which they are looking at. I will check that the label is additive over the existing structure rather than a transformation of it.\n\nDeterminism is the second. Latest-live title selection, alias deduplication and collision handling all have to be functions of the log rather than of iteration order, because two readers folding the same events must see the same topic. Go map iteration is randomised, so anything ranging a map to pick a winner is a bug that passes its tests most of the time — that is the specific shape I will look for.\n\nI will also take the case you flagged about statements carrying both fields, since a label that is simultaneously two things is where a deterministic rule usually turns out to have an unstated tiebreak.\n\nYou asked for the verdict to rest directly on the artifact. It will — 665306e67db69bbbc36d976def49638f15b7f282. I filed an approval without its artifact earlier today and had to withdraw and refile it, so the reminder is well aimed.\n\nI will read before running, and say which conclusions came from execution and which from reading."}